Package: tt-gozer
Architecture: all
Depends: ${python3:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Suggests: tt-smi
Description: cooperative Tenstorrent chip leasing for shared boxes
 gozer lets several agents and people share one machine with Tenstorrent
 accelerators. A workload takes a lease on one or more boards before it opens
 /dev/tenstorrent/*, and gives it back when it is done. Leases are checked
 against the open file descriptors of real processes, so a crashed workload
 does not hold a board forever. Requests that cannot be met are queued.
 .
 The package also ships three Claude Code skills and gozer-install-skills,
 which links them into the calling user's ~/.claude/skills. Resetting chips
 needs tt-smi; leasing does not.
